This fork (https://github.com/backnotprop/artifact-fs) adds a macOS front
end for the Pando FSKit extension: the package internal/fskit and the wire
contract docs/pando-fskit-wire-v3.md.

Parts of internal/fskit are translated to Go from Oak's FSKit backend
(https://oak.space/oak/oak, mirror https://github.com/oakdotspace/oak),
Copyright Oakspace Inc. and the Oak contributors, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0 (the same text as LICENSE). Source:
cli/src/commands/mount/fskit/ (protocol.rs, ipc.rs, server.rs, mod.rs) at
commit 8d35309d4187dfceefe03a74cf4612c179ab524e (2026-09-27). Oak's licence
covers its code; Oak's name and logo are not used.

What was translated, and how it changed (Apache 2.0, section 4(b)):

- protocol.rs and ipc.rs: the length-prefixed request and reply framing
  became wire version 3 (a u32 frame length, a u32 header length, a JSON
  header with request ids, raw payload bytes), with 15 operations:
  setattr replaces truncate; symlink and forget are new; readdir is paged.
  The accept loop blocks instead of polling, and each connection carries
  many requests at once.
- server.rs: per-operation dispatch, rewritten over ArtifactFS's Resolver
  and Engine, with an inode table (root 2, others from 3, stable per path),
  removed items kept until forget, EEXIST for create, mkdir and symlink,
  directory verifiers, and a per-operation errno mapping.
- mod.rs: the macOS mount driver (internal/fskit/mount_darwin.go): running
  /sbin/mount -F for the FSKit volume, refusing to run as root, checking
  the extension with pluginkit, and turning mount failures (an extension
  that is off or missing, a privacy-protected folder) into plain
  instructions.
